# __APP_NAME__

__PURPOSE__

This is the editable Unity empty template. It includes:

- a local web surface;
- an agent boundary with its prompt in `src/agent/prompts/system.md`;
- an AI Gateway configuration seam;
- exactly one intentionally empty Hosted Skill at `src/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/`;
- whole-app `dev-start` and `dev-stop` scripts.

The template does not invent domain tools. Implement the Hosted Skill directly in
source or open it in Intelligent Function App Studio.

## Run

Unity Studio automatically selects available ports before opening a newly
created app. Assignments are saved in `.unity-studio/ports.env`, excluding both
live listeners and other apps' saved ports. Existing apps are not stopped or
reassigned.

Start the agent and web preview without requiring Azure Functions Core Tools:

### macOS/Linux

```bash
./scripts/dev-start.sh --skip-skill
```

### PowerShell 7

```powershell
.\scripts\dev-start.ps1 -SkipSkill
```

Open the web URL printed by startup or shown in **Run/Debug**. Both platforms
load the saved ports; do not assume the web app uses port 3000. For an app created
outside Studio with no saved settings, the defaults are web 3000, agent 8088,
and skill 7071.

Stop this app with:

### macOS/Linux

```bash
./scripts/dev-stop.sh
```

### PowerShell 7

```powershell
.\scripts\dev-stop.ps1
```

The startup script uses the Microsoft Python package mirror and starts the local
mock agent and web surface. To include the Hosted Skill, install Azure Functions
Core Tools first, then omit `--skip-skill` / `-SkipSkill`.
